# ChkTeX settings for this repo. ChkTeX reads this file on top of the default
# and the global ~/.chktexrc: LaTeX Workshop passes it with -l on its own, and
# on the command line run `chktex -l .chktexrc <file>` (or run chktex from the
# repo root, where it finds ./.chktexrc by itself).
#
# Each block below adds to ChkTeX's built-in list unless it says otherwise.

# Warning 38 ("You should not use punctuation in front of quotes") wants
# British placement. This text is US English, which puts periods and commas
# inside the quotes. The global ~/.chktexrc says the same; it is repeated here
# so the repo lints the same way on a machine without it.
CmdLine
{
    -n38
}

# Arguments that hold no English prose, so ChkTeX should not lint them:
# Hebrew, Greek, and Syriac text; the headword and the quoted entry of a HALOT
# note; the references (book, chapter, verse); and the Latin abbreviations of
# the BHS critical apparatus, which is the first argument of \ca. The second
# argument of \ca is the English gloss, so it is still checked.
#
# The leading [] is not a real optional argument. It lets ChkTeX skip the
# argument count in each \newcommand line of bible.tex, such as
# \newcommand\Hebrew[1]{...}, which it would otherwise flag as a solo `]'.
WipeArg
{
    \Hebrew:[]{} \Greek:[]{} \Syriac:[]{}
    \halot:[]{}{} \halotu:[]{}{}
    \haref:[]{}{}{} \vref:[]{}{}{} \caref:[]{}{}{}
    \ca:[]{}
}

# Commands that want a `~' in front of them. This replaces the built-in list
# to drop \vref: here it is a scripture reference (Gen 1:1), not the varioref
# page reference, so a normal space before it is fine.
Linker =
{
    \ref \pageref \eqref \cite
}

# Commands that print no word of their own, so the space after them is
# meant to be swallowed: the poetry indents, the inline poetry space, the
# thin space, and the Hebrew, Greek, and Syriac font switches. \ae sits in
# the middle of a word (Aram\ae an), where the space only ends the command.
#
# Word-like macros such as \lord and the sigla (\septuagint, \peshitta, and
# the rest) are left out on purpose: a space after them is swallowed too, so
# a warning there is a real missing `\ '.
Silent
{
    \pa \pb \pc \pd \pe \ilsp
    \thinspace
    \sblh \sblg \sbls \abbrev
    \ae
}
